Description: Always require reline/io/ansi so Reline::ANSI is defined
 When TERM=dumb (common in autopkgtest/schroot/CI), decide_io_gate only
 loads Reline::Dumb and skips requiring reline/io/ansi. IRB tests then
 load Reline first; later Reline::ANSITest calls ANSI.new and fails with
 NameError. Always require the ANSI backend (as already done for Dumb)
 so the constant exists regardless of TERM at first require.
Author: Simon Quigley <tsimonq2@debian.org>
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/lib/reline/io.rb
+++ b/lib/reline/io.rb
@@ -53,3 +53,4 @@ module Reline
 end
 
 require 'reline/io/dumb'
+require 'reline/io/ansi'
